Read the inactive titlebar colours into the palette

The palette carried the active titlebar pair of the window manager
group alone. A sheet that paints an inactive window frame needs the
other pair of that group. A fallback to the window colours gives a
value to a scheme that names neither key.

The read mirrors the active pair, key for key. No GTK sheet reads the
new members, so the four shipped sheets keep their bytes.

The change sits on the branch work/firefox-theme of the local tree, as
commit 2 of 14. The branch holds those fourteen commits above the head of
work/gtk4-theme, which merge request !15 on system/qtcurve holds. The fork
wyn/qtcurve holds work/firefox-theme. Merge request !29 on system/qtcurve
holds that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/gtk4/writer/palette.cpp b/gtk4/writer/palette.cpp
index 22f14cb0..1ad85873 100644
--- a/gtk4/writer/palette.cpp
+++ b/gtk4/writer/palette.cpp
@@ -350,6 +350,9 @@ readPalette(const QString &file, const Options &opts, Palette &pal,
     const KConfigGroup wm(cfg, QStringLiteral("WM"));
     pal.titlebar = wm.readEntry("activeBackground", pal.window);
     pal.titlebarText = wm.readEntry("activeForeground", pal.windowText);
+    pal.titlebarInactive = wm.readEntry("inactiveBackground", pal.window);
+    pal.titlebarInactiveText = wm.readEntry("inactiveForeground",
+                                            pal.windowText);
 
     shadeLadder(opts, pal.button, pal.btn);
     shadeLadder(opts, pal.base, pal.bgnd);
diff --git a/gtk4/writer/palette.h b/gtk4/writer/palette.h
index d7d5a85d..eb618bb0 100644
--- a/gtk4/writer/palette.h
+++ b/gtk4/writer/palette.h
@@ -54,6 +54,8 @@ struct Palette {
     QColor tooltip, tooltipText;
     QColor link, negative, neutral, positive;
     QColor titlebar, titlebarText;
+    /** The inactive titlebar pair, which no GTK sheet reads. */
+    QColor titlebarInactive, titlebarInactiveText;
     Shades btn, bgnd, win, hl, menu;
     bool dark = false;
 };
